    {
      "id": "Zulu6dWTCK5NWRAHpc2D5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5529.4794044725595,
      "y": 2637.2570003162036,
      "width": 739.4367675781269,
      "height": 1125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "fpkpRBSbYlX1Fl7_i_yOa",
        "wR1nj31ahClh4MM8O87rN",
        "f0q_4nyAVvWVdz1ygE2aU"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 772977978,
      "version": 4773,
      "versionNonce": 287055452,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790705154925,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Each column represents the tokens for a given step in the joint sequence\nGiven two streams of audios, they simply apply the acoustic delay to both,\nand concatenate them into one representation.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMoshi also model the textual representation of its own speech (Inner\nDialogue)\nMore precisely, Helium, its pretrained text language-model backbone,\npredicts a text token first, and then uses it as part of the conditioning\nfor generating the corresponding semantic/acoustic speech tokens.\n\nPutting together the multi-stream and inner monologue, we have the final\nset V of sequences to model defined as\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nwhen the user speaks and Moshi stays silent, the corresponding audio\ntokens for Moshi’s stream decode into “natural silence”, a near silent\nwaveform, instead of having a fixed, well defined value; At the same time,\nMoshi’s text stream will be filled with PAD tokens.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Each column represents the tokens for a given step in the joint sequence\nGiven two streams of audios, they simply apply the acoustic delay to both, \nand concatenate them into one representation.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMoshi also model the textual representation of its own speech (Inner Dialogue)\nMore precisely, Helium, its pretrained text language-model backbone, predicts a text token first, and then uses it as part of the conditioning for generating the corresponding semantic/acoustic speech tokens.\n\nPutting together the multi-stream and inner monologue, we have the final set V of sequences to model defined as\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nwhen the user speaks and Moshi stays silent, the corresponding audio tokens for Moshi’s stream decode into “natural silence”, a near silent waveform, instead of having a fixed, well defined value; At the same time, Moshi’s text stream will be filled with PAD tokens.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790499672085,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
