      ],
      "crop": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AJJqQGpkoM97BkeffS0Sz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6498.055226645188,
      "y": 5394.926631000584,
      "width": 511.51641845703125,
      "height": 480,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HB3lPkbGRL3MkwOy3VvgU",
        "jPIQ6GhCUy3rAP5LJKicB",
        "s5byTBW6_dZyFPP5kfKHS"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1531110394,
      "version": 505,
      "versionNonce": 1117207908,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790705154925,
      "created": 1790501652905,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WavLM jointly learns masked speech prediction and denoising in\npre-training. \nMasked speech prediction: parts of the input speech\nrepresentation are hidden, and the model must infer what should\nbe there from the surrounding context\n\n                        Speech:   A   B   C   D   E\n                        Mask:     A   B  [X]  D   E\n                                          ↓\n                                     predict C\n\nDenoising: the input audio is deliberately corrupted, for example\nby adding noise or mixing in speech from another speaker, while\nthe training target still corresponds to the original clean speech.\n\n                            Clean speech\n                                 +\n                            noise / interfering speaker\n                                 ↓\n                            corrupted input\n                                 ↓\n                               WavLM\n                                 ↓\n                            representation of the original speech",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WavLM jointly learns masked speech prediction and denoising in pre-training. \nMasked speech prediction: parts of the input speech representation are hidden, and the model must infer what should be there from the surrounding context\n\n                        Speech:   A   B   C   D   E\n                        Mask:     A   B  [X]  D   E\n                                          ↓\n                                     predict C\n\nDenoising: the input audio is deliberately corrupted, for example by adding noise or mixing in speech from another speaker, while the training target still corresponds to the original clean speech.\n\n                            Clean speech\n                                 +\n                            noise / interfering speaker\n                                 ↓\n                            corrupted input\n                                 ↓\n                               WavLM\n                                 ↓\n                            representation of the original speech",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
