    {
      "id": "B-xOJJf84hyuYjZnOrF_Q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7004.867458957767,
      "y": 506.766969799497,
      "width": 980.3690185546875,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "4Wdid0ZwDWYXR-dZqKqFr",
        "FC40f9qyPZ9CMsdu74Eo0",
        "iwXMWqSp3m0eBNJNP6Dqw"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b30",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 660250810,
      "version": 5650,
      "versionNonce": 1084656476,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790712338556,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "PersonaPlex is a duplex-style multimodal model that follows the Moshi architecture by receiving\nthree input streams: user audio, agent text, and agent audio but adds two capabilities Moshi\nlargely lacked: explicit role conditioning and zero-shot voice conditioning.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Hybrid System Prompt consists of two temporally concatenated segments: a text prompt\nsegment and a voice prompt segment. The text prompt segment performs role conditioning by\nforcing scenario-specific text tokens on the agent text channel while keeping the agent audio\nchannel silent. The voice prompt segment performs voice prompting by supplying a short speech\nsample on the agent audio channel while padding the agent text channel.\n\nWe train PersonaPlex by first initializing neural network\nweights to those of Moshi [2], followed by fine-tuning using\nour hybrid system prompt on synthetic dialogs\nThe full training\ndataset has 1840 hours of customer service dialog interactions\nacross 105,410 dialogs, and 410 hours of general Question-\nAnswering dialogs across 39,322 dialogs. Training takes 6 hours\non 8xA100 GPUs.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "PersonaPlex is a duplex-style multimodal model that follows the Moshi architecture by receiving three input streams: user audio, agent text, and agent audio but adds two capabilities Moshi largely lacked: explicit role conditioning and zero-shot voice conditioning.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Hybrid System Prompt consists of two temporally concatenated segments: a text prompt segment and a voice prompt segment. The text prompt segment performs role conditioning by forcing scenario-specific text tokens on the agent text channel while keeping the agent audio channel silent. The voice prompt segment performs voice prompting by supplying a short speech sample on the agent audio channel while padding the agent text channel.\n\nWe train PersonaPlex by first initializing neural network\nweights to those of Moshi [2], followed by fine-tuning using\nour hybrid system prompt on synthetic dialogs\nThe full training\ndataset has 1840 hours of customer service dialog interactions\nacross 105,410 dialogs, and 410 hours of general Question-\nAnswering dialogs across 39,322 dialogs. Training takes 6 hours\non 8xA100 GPUs.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790505337528,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
