      "text": "Semantic VAD",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Semantic VAD",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gcUeQeqC7fRvGNr_yoRXH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7802.079362629913,
      "y": 1939.8784136630456,
      "width": 788.4047328404013,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "vhgbGHh_undOSuwtj2Rok",
        "5CDFB22jz9RqYBP1JnUYy",
        "WkU1pekR7aFle54Hvp6vs",
        "x9BoR4EvhYBcCl3O_m-Lo",
        "gXP-WWcUBkH6H40qPYn-S"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 427316188,
      "version": 6028,
      "versionNonce": 1847088100,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790709433527,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A traditional VAD waits until the silence after speech lasts a fixed maximum, for\nexample 700 ms.\nThe key insight: if the silence comes right after a complete sentence, you can\ndecide much sooner.\n\nThe model has four parts:\n    - Speech encoder that turns the audio into a vector representation for each\n        frame\n    - Punctuation prediction. For each frame, a classifier predicts one of three\n        classes: no punctuation, ending punctuation (a period or question mark,\n        meaning the thought is complete), or non-ending punctuation (a comma,\n        meaning the thought is incomplete).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A traditional VAD waits until the silence after speech lasts a fixed maximum, for example 700 ms.\nThe key insight: if the silence comes right after a complete sentence, you can decide much sooner.\n\nThe model has four parts:\n    - Speech encoder that turns the audio into a vector representation for each\n        frame\n    - Punctuation prediction. For each frame, a classifier predicts one of three\n        classes: no punctuation, ending punctuation (a period or question mark,\n        meaning the thought is complete), or non-ending punctuation (a comma,\n        meaning the thought is incomplete).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790707289833,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
