      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Training DuplexSLA",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Training DuplexSLA",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JyglSif4LTT1las0pIOY4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8810.331398520484,
      "y": 4875.1017748434715,
      "width": 980.3690185546875,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "qtQ8yt67_J8sQSHF18MM9",
        "B9aytQ6ANLX45NMAr3sit",
        "5lpNpf9W6qO9k-9C_bZ3P",
        "tiaGJb4fV-PeVAlVL60nL",
        "ua7iX7wJFaBecmm_n3fpv"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b40",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 322622180,
      "version": 5916,
      "versionNonce": 541140580,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790711049819,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Normal dialogue datasets don't have the chunk-by-chunk, three-channel format, so the authors built\nthe data themselves (Figure 4 of the paper):\n\n    - Annotation by an LLM: raw text dialogues were given to an LLM, which added tool calls at the\n        right points: function name, arguments, planning text, and the exact moment in the\n        conversation where the action should happen.\n    - Speech synthesis: user and assistant lines were turned into audio with text-to-speech and\n        voice cloning, with 18 main assistant voices.\n    - Alignment: the audio was force-aligned so every word has a precise timestamp, then everything\n        was cut into 160 ms chunks, and each label or tool call was placed in the chunk where it\n        should occur.\n\nDuplexSLA starts from Step-Audio 2 mini, a 7B audio language model that already understands and\ngenerates speech.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Normal dialogue datasets don't have the chunk-by-chunk, three-channel format, so the authors built the data themselves (Figure 4 of the paper):\n\n    - Annotation by an LLM: raw text dialogues were given to an LLM, which added tool calls at the\n        right points: function name, arguments, planning text, and the exact moment in the\n        conversation where the action should happen.\n    - Speech synthesis: user and assistant lines were turned into audio with text-to-speech and\n        voice cloning, with 18 main assistant voices.\n    - Alignment: the audio was force-aligned so every word has a precise timestamp, then everything\n        was cut into 160 ms chunks, and each label or tool call was placed in the chunk where it\n        should occur.\n\nDuplexSLA starts from Step-Audio 2 mini, a 7B audio language model that already understands and generates speech.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1790710158933,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
